{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">2025 AMC 10B #4</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12B #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Not_too_bad-_Simple_Modular_Arithmetic_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Not too bad- Simple Modular Arithmetic Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:40)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of the two-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9eeaaa9b634cda4ea52fcf726ca143421db524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a}~\\underline{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> in base seven equals the value of the two-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee2600ebf093705a1c70f5724734db3b6e66769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{b}~\\underline{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> in base nine. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917cdf8efc9c4864345e3c006cc837fec14e7cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5054075c16c4008fe84167b8fd415258ec349f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~7\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~9\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~10\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~11\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By definition of bases, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9eeaaa9b634cda4ea52fcf726ca143421db524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a}~\\underline{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> base seven is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/73453c88b70bd11e5341fe946596f0490a96c4a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee2600ebf093705a1c70f5724734db3b6e66769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{b}~\\underline{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> base nine is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5277149d798ff700548358639810159d5553a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd52ac6c75fbc57b75b1dcccaf28cfbd1f0c409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7a+b=9b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2cf2d695cedcf556bb21dbd0747a3556f7bc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6a=8b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411466544341a0f600f573b4f8eb0e860622c0a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a=4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. This means e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1cb96a3344461b85f9e6eb91850987abd720a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer), and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are coprime, it follows simply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a336d9f5d6ead525f7e9d9e757252fe62393214a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e6a48fa27a3cfd891e3720d4cc76428e6ef60f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b = 3a = 3 \\cdot 4k \\iff b = 3k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"232\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. the integer solutions are parametrised by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083ca1d083f6d594171d4e2fd3b9de237a391b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (4k,3k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, but of course in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/35245a0f2eb0765cadfed783d95a019720fb40ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7ffa3b8792f0170bce1ab6008e907343100d70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> as the only solution. Thus their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f49f04c43b81fd30b91ef53394c9d7730b91f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 4+3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"186\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ CW\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The first equation comes from the following idea. In base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, a two-digit number can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the tens digit plus the units digit, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44efece41f511b94e1f1316b848064d07bdd5d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^1 \\cdot a + 10^0 \\cdot b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. If we insert the base numbers into this expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9eeaaa9b634cda4ea52fcf726ca143421db524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a}~\\underline{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee2600ebf093705a1c70f5724734db3b6e66769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{b}~\\underline{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b4cd57a75cf88c77244bc01830d64d1af93503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^1 \\cdot a + b = 9^1 \\cdot b + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />. The rest of the solution is above.\n</p><p>Note that this method applies to any number of digits as well as decimals.\n~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both digits base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, they must be from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92b949e93a365184a38b536f357290abfd2810f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> must be strictly greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> because two-digit representations in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> exceed the values of those in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Starting from testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, we see that the combination <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320ba30eff066d894e7018df0a84bafebdecef5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b) = (4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies the condition. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5f9945f124e17e81a2b738fcb5b2a1e0eccd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~megaboy6679\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Not_too_bad-_Simple_Modular_Arithmetic_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Not_too_bad-_Simple_Modular_Arithmetic_Bash)\">Solution 3 (Not too bad- Simple Modular Arithmetic Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Not too bad- Simple Modular Arithmetic Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We interpret the two-digit numbers literally:\n</p><p>In base 7:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb343c0770705d855f301f0d437777b5cf2520a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{a} \\ \\overline{b} = 7a + b.\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\nIn base 9:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9ddb8dda9bd0f7b7287b46ac191f3fa86b95a5dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{b} \\ \\overline{a} = 9b + a.\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\nThe condition is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bbf41ada01466526ac616c57116159b8c864f85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7a + b = 9b + a.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />\nWe want \\( a + b \\), but we will milk modular arithmetic as much as possible.\n</p><p>Start with the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bbf41ada01466526ac616c57116159b8c864f85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7a + b = 9b + a.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />\nRearrange:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/2830a7cc43791647274d4102031048d00a16e2f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7a - a = 9b - b,\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c858eed96da66c3342cd660b3b88876600d7bf5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6a = 8b,\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d540f6ff568b0f2db55eed0355f9f0febbb931ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a = 4b.\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />\nThis already says \\( \\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{4}{3} \\).\nBut instead of finishing, we now do highly unnecessary modular analysis.\n</p><p>First, reduce the equation modulo 3:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279604527bf9c01b1caaeb28ea8025f1c13645d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a - 4b \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}.\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\nCompute residues:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be247c9b41d31905555e74f4668a569db4c29103.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\text{ always.}\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d74df86e120fb75edd7f70678dfdc7e649cb3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4b \\equiv b \\pmod{3}.\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />\nSo:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd6d62e648491a7e5372c5c42f4e3cdc7036ab5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 - b \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\Rightarrow b \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" />\nThus \\( b \\in \\{0, 3, 6\\} \\) (since digits in base 7 must be \\( 0 \\le b \\le 6 \\)).\n</p><p>Now reduce the same equation modulo 4:\n</p><p>Original condition \\( 3a = 4b \\).\nModulo 4:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a9eb164aeee85cb3c8a4e650d7b89fdd3c7f0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\nSince \\( \\gcd(3, 4) = 1 \\), the multiplicative inverse of 3 modulo 4 is 3, because\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b857f79402641f85df13d9a01cd30c915dbc12ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 \\cdot 3 = 9 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />\nMultiply both sides of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abfc46a808e824d9a905294756bfecf4a2ba2a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />\nby 3:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/43795bf76bc7922e06c0c3a111adcdee35e50f08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}.\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />\nThus \\( a \\in \\{0, 4\\} \\), because digits in base 7 satisfy \\( 0 \\le a \\le 6 \\).\n</p><p>We now have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88ee4c1abc4c0722f950b7ee93528625f0be8b7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\in \\{0, 4\\}, b \\in \\{0, 3, 6\\}.\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />\nNext impose the original equation \\( 3a = 4b \\) exactly, not just modularly.\n</p><p>Test combinations:\n</p><p>\\( a = 0 \\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7e2699746f43d5749b26dc49e8f46a3feb17f60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a = 0, 4b = 4b.\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />\nFor equality we need \\( b = 0 \\).\nThat gives \\( (a, b) = (0, 0) \\), but this represents the “two-digit” numbers \\( 00_7 \\) and \\( 00_9 \\).\nTechnically valid but trivial; we check the problem expectation: since it asks “What is \\( a + b \\)?”, zero is possible but let's check the other option.\n</p><p>\\( a = 4 \\):\nSolve\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bcc26b43de382dc9062051d60f8d140e47ce2fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 \\cdot 4 = 4b,\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd00f8e9cbe5c39f5bad21ab4235da18a971b72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12 = 4b,\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694511c052e47c7e7bb6371a37ebba452f284662.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b = 3.\\]\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />\nCheck that digits are valid:\n</p><p>\\( a = 4 \\) is allowed in base 7.\n</p><p>\\( b = 3 \\) is allowed in base 7 and base 9.\n</p><p>Now confirm the original equation explicitly using base values:\n</p><p>Left side (base 7 number \\( \\overline{ab} \\)):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a8353c4fdb06bb7fae2c403375291cc46e19e541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7a + b = 7 \\cdot 4 + 3 = 28 + 3 = 31.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"14\" />\nRight side (base 9 number \\( \\overline{ba} \\)):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/596b7eba336a60568d4a2b3a1aeb2f162d48b638.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9b + a = 9 \\cdot 3 + 4 = 27 + 4 = 31.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"14\" />\nEquality holds.\n</p><p>Thus the nontrivial valid solution is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e490fb012ca3fa9c561053f03521eab8e359e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a, b) = (4, 3).\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />\nCompute:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f820f0a94a443e30f0ad21ce0af3461701d374.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b = 4 + 3 = 7.\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />\nFinal answer:\n\\( 7 \\).\n</p><p>~notvalid\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Fast)\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write both integers as linear expressions and equate them\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371cc7a59077e64bcfa503ae63641c9a849da890.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7a+b = 9b+a\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />\nTo find solutions to this, we can put everything on one side so it equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2c26c3077bca6565265f844890b4cc10286327.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6a-8b=0\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" />\nNow, assuming a coordinate form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> you can quite easily see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/869dc1459f793eaf7e933289a7fa2a13673b8f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution. However, this violates the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are less than 7. You can see that just taking half of them gets you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563948106c3332662355412547d99acab218c16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and that no other solution would work without exceeding, so, the answer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5f9945f124e17e81a2b738fcb5b2a1e0eccd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~shockfront99\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:40.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:40)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto\">https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pOTAw6MZCuw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pOTAw6MZCuw</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uIAAy7jvE8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4uIAAy7jvE8</a>\n~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B\">2025 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\